  "description": "The proposal seeks planning permission for the change of use of an existing dwellinghouse (Use Class C3) to a small-scale children’s residential care home (Use Class C2).\n\nThe development will accommodate a maximum of three children aged between 8–17 years, supported by non-resident care staff operating on a shift basis, including one sleep-in staff member overnight.\n\nThe proposal involves internal alterations only to facilitate the use, including the provision of:\n\nThree children’s bedrooms\nOne staff bedroom / sleep-in room\nStaff office space\nCommunal living, dining and kitchen areas\nBathroom and WC facilities\n\nNo external extensions or alterations are proposed, and the external appearance of the building will remain unchanged.\n\nThe existing single off-street parking space will be retained, with no changes to the front garden layout. Secure cycle storage and refuse storage will be provided within the site.\n\nThe use will operate in a domestic manner consistent with a typical family household, with appropriate management arrangements in place as set out within the accompanying Management Plan.",
